stages.sampleAnswer:
- Job: { id, name, schedule (cron/timestamp), timeout, maxRetries, createdAt, updatedAt }
- Execution: { id, jobId, scheduledTime, startTime?, endTime?, status (queued/running/success/failed/timeout), result?, error?, attempt }
- Lease: { jobId, workerId, leaseExpiresAt } — held by a worker to claim a job.
- IdempotencyKey: { jobId, executionId, idempotencyKeyHash } — used to detect and skip duplicate requests.

POST /jobs
  body: { name: 'str', schedule: 'cron | timestamp', timeout: ms, maxRetries: int, config: {...} }
  → 201 { jobId }

GET /jobs/:jobId → { id, name, schedule, status, lastExecutionTime?, nextExecutionTime? }

GET /jobs/:jobId/executions → [ { id, status, scheduledTime, startTime, endTime, attempt } ]

GET /executions/:executionId → { id, jobId, status, output?, error?, logs? }

POST /jobs/:jobId/pause → 200
